    steps: ["Proposal: under Payments tap Add deposit and enter the amount, date and method once you receive it. The proposal shows Deposit paid and Balance after deposit.", "When the client approves (or you tap Create invoice), the deposit is copied onto the invoice once as a payment, so Still owed is already reduced. With card payments on, the client can tap Approve & pay deposit $X, or Approve now, pay the deposit another way.", "Deposit came in after you made the invoice? Record it on the proposal; it carries over to the first invoice as long as that invoice isn't paid yet.", "Each proposal has one invoice. If you tap Create invoice when one already exists, you'll see 'This proposal already has an invoice (INV-…). Opening it now.' and it opens that invoice, so the deposit is never copied twice. A new invoice is only allowed if the earlier one was voided.", "Invoice: under Payment stages (optional), tap Add stage and set its type to Deposit (Amount or Percent, plus a Due date). Online card payments charge the deposit stage first."],
